# `new Map(..)` | `new Set(..)` over a written list of constants is made of the record of the list, which goes into the image: a table where the entries are primitives, else a tree.
# The table of the image holds an object only where its fields stand in front of its other names. Where it does not, the construction as written runs on the list that code builds
# f1 = oddKeyInMap, f2 = oddKeyInSet, f3 = oddKeyOneListDeeper: no record. f4 = namesInMap, f5 = indexInFrontOfName, f6 = primitivesInSet: still the record
